# TRANSOVO STANDARDS — MANDATORY FOR ALL WORK (ALWAYS)

The 15 standards in `.cursor/rules/transovo-*.mdc` (backed by `docs/TRANSOVO-*.md`) are **HARD REQUIREMENTS** for **every change** in this repository — not optional design guides.

## Scope (everything)

These rules apply when you touch **any** of:

- New or existing **pages**, routes, layouts, components (`src/app/`, `src/components/`, `src/kimi-ui/`)
- **API routes**, server actions, webhooks (`src/app/api/`)
- **Business logic** (`src/lib/`)
- **Database** schema, migrations, Prisma models (when they affect user-visible behavior, consent, auth, or data rights)
- **Workers**, jobs, queues, cron (`src/lib/jobs/`, BullMQ handlers)
- **Scripts** that change product behavior or customer data
- **Nav**, entitlements, product flags (`src/lib/products/`)

**UI-only guides** (visual, responsive, page layout) still bind whenever you ship or change a customer-facing surface. **Backend-heavy guides** (security, privacy/consent, datetime, i18n, forms validation) bind on APIs and lib code even when no JSX changes.

## You MUST (every task)

1. Treat **all 15** Transovo standards as binding — read the **full source doc** for each guide that applies to your change.
2. Read `docs/TRANSOVO-PRODUCT-DESIGN-UX-GOVERNANCE.md` first for authority order and conflict resolution.
3. Before a **new page or feature**: check IA (Guide #3), page archetype (page architecture), HCD workflow fit (Guide #2), and runtime truth (settings must work).
4. Before **API/backend** work: security/auth (Guide #9), privacy/consent (Guide #8), forms/validation (Guide #5), datetime (Guide #10), i18n (Guide #11) as applicable.
5. Follow **authority order** when documents conflict.
6. Fix **shared systems** — never one-off patches that bypass tokens, components, or canonical engines.
7. Ensure **visible UI reflects actual runtime** — no fake toggles, no dead settings, no mock success in production paths.

## You MUST NOT

- Ship any page, API, or feature without considering **all applicable** standards guides.
- Invent features, nav homes, terminology, or consent flows outside approved scope.
- Treat `docs/TRANSOVO-*` or `.cursor/rules/transovo-*` as reference-only.
- Skip security, privacy, or consent rules because the task "is backend only."

